PART 4 -- the crossing staircase: order-cell cost per step position
================================================================================================
  pair (i,j) of speeds crosses |v_i - v_j| times per period (difference uniformity);
  a step at sorted position l is straddled by (l)(13-l) pairs + the 0-runner pairs:
  AP {1..13} (with 0): total pair crossings per period = 455
  triangle weights l(14-l) for l=1..13: [13, 24, 33, 40, 45, 48, 49, 48, 45, 40, 33, 24, 13]  (middle steps cost most)
  sum of weights = 455  (should equal total crossings for unit steps: 455)

DONE.

